{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>For now I know</b> — At first his fear was in potential; it had not yet emerged into actuality in this great deed. But now it has become known through its performance, so his merit is complete, and his reward from before HaShem, the Elohim of Israel, shall be complete. And the meaning of the passage, that \"the Elohim\" is the One who tests and commands in the Binding (Akedah), while \"the angel of YHWH\" is the one who prevents and promises, will be clarified by the verse \"the angel who redeems me\" (Genesis 48:16)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase 'ודעת הפרשה' is rendered as 'the meaning of the passage,' referring to the conceptual understanding of the pericope."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:14.021607808Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}